  "extraction_notes": "[text-pass] The AgSbTe2 is added as nanoinclusions to the Yb0.2Co4Sb12 matrix. The doping of the matrix by Te is inferred from carrier concentration changes. [figure-pass p1-5] The paper describes nanocomposites of Yb0.2Co4Sb12 with AgSbTe2 inclusions. The AgSbTe2 inclusions act as a source of Te doping into the skutterudite matrix. Seebeck coefficient values at 300 K were extracted from Fig. 6 and the body text. [figure-pass p6-7] The samples are composites of Yb0.2Co4Sb12 matrix with AgSbTe2 nanoparticles. The AgSbTe2 is treated as a secondary phase/nanoinclusion rather than a traditional dopant substituting into the lattice sites of the matrix. ",
  "status": "ok",
